1. INVENTION FAMILY — BBIS
============================================================

Working Name:

Boundary-to-Boundary Invariant Survival

Short Description:

A governance property and associated implementation mechanisms for
maintaining an enforceable governing invariant across mutation-capable
execution boundaries until the actual irreversible mutation authority.

Core Question:

Can a governing invariant survive every mutation-capable boundary until
the irreversible mutation authority?

Potential Technical Subject:

- canonical governing state
- mutation-capable boundary identification
- boundary-local verification
- invariant propagation
- invariant recomputation
- refusal semantics
- commit-point enforcement
- alternate-path enforcement
- retry/recovery enforcement
- final-boundary enforcement

Existing Evidence:

- OWASP engagement
